{"title": "Sectional Mock #53 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>Find the total number of smaller cubes obtained if half of a cube which has a side of 18 cm is cut into smaller cubes of 1 cm each and the other half of that cube is cut into smaller cubes of 3 cm each?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; 1 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; 3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["2300", "4890", "3024", "1250"], "options_hi": ["2300", "4890", "3024", "1250"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>The side of the cube is 18 cm and the sides of the smaller cubes are either 1 cm or 3 cm.</p><p>Volume of original cube = 18 * 18 * 18 = 5832.</p><p>Half of the cube will be a rectangular cuboid.</p><p>Hence, volume of one rectangular cuboid = 9 * 18 * 18 = 2916</p><p>Volume of smaller cube having length of 1 cm = 1 * 1 * 1 = 1.</p><p>The number of cubes having length of 1 cm = 2916/1 = 2916.</p><p>Volume of smaller cube having length of 3 cm = 3 * 3 * 3 = 27.</p><p>The number of cubes having length of 3 cm = 2916/27 = 108.</p><p>The total number of smaller cubes = 2916 + 108 = 3024.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The side of the cube is 18 cm and the sides of the smaller cubes are either 1 cm or 3 cm.</p><p>Volume of original cube = 18 * 18 * 18 = 5832.</p><p>Half of the cube will be a rectangular cuboid.</p><p>Hence, volume of one rectangular cuboid = 9 * 18 * 18 = 2916</p><p>Volume of smaller cube having length of 1 cm = 1 * 1 * 1 = 1.</p><p>The number of cubes having length of 1 cm = 2916/1 = 2916.</p><p>Volume of smaller cube having length of 3 cm = 3 * 3 * 3 = 27.</p><p>The number of cubes having length of 3 cm = 2916/27 = 108.</p><p>The total number of smaller cubes = 2916 + 108 = 3024.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A is inversely proportional to B and inversely proportional to square of C. When B = 20 and C = 2&radic;2, then A = 24. What will be the value of C when A = 32, and B = 9?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; B = 20 &#2324;&#2352; C = 2&radic;2 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; A = 24 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A = 32 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; B = 9 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; C &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["&radic;10/3", "2&radic;(10/3)", "2&radic;5", "&radic;5/3"], "options_hi": ["&radic;10/3", "2&radic;(10/3)", "2&radic;5", "&radic;5/3"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=61 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=60 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image003.png\"></p><p>K=3840</p><p>Now,</p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=57 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=67 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image006.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=61 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=60 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image003.png\"></p><p>K=3840</p><p>Now,</p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=57 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=67 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image006.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>If A = 10<sup>400</sup>, B = 8<sup>200</sup>, and C = 6<sup>800</sup>, then which of the following is true?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A = 10<sup>400</sup>, B = 8<sup>200</sup>, &#2324;&#2352; C = 6<sup>800</sup>, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["A &lt; B &lt; C", "C &lt; A &lt; B", "B &lt; A &lt; C", "A &lt; C &lt; B"], "options_hi": ["A &lt; B &lt; C", "C &lt; A &lt; B", "B &lt; A &lt; C", "A &lt; C &lt; B"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=201 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=159 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=111 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image009.png\"></p><p>Therefore, B &lt; A &lt; C</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=201 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=159 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=111 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image009.png\"></p><p>Therefore, B &lt; A &lt; C</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the difference between the sum of prime numbers between 30 and 40 to the sum of prime number between 40 and 50?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>30 &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 40 &#2324;&#2352; 50 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["64", "65", "63", "61"], "options_hi": ["64", "65", "63", "61"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>For perfect cube, number of zeroes should be 3, 6, 9 etc.</p><p>(a) 1000000, since it has 6 zeroes, so cube root = 10<sup>3</sup></p><p>(b) 2160000 - 4 zeroes</p><p>(c) 194000 = 194 * 1000 =&gt; 194 is not a perfect cube)</p><p>(d) 12500000  -  5 zeroes</p><p>Hence, option 'a' is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>For perfect cube, number of zeroes should be 3, 6, 9 etc.</p><p>(a) 1000000, since it has 6 zeroes, so cube root = 10<sup>3</sup></p><p>(b) 2160000 - 4 zeroes</p><p>(c) 194000 = 194 * 1000 =&gt; 194 is not a perfect cube)</p><p>(d) 12500000  -  5 zeroes</p><p>Hence, option 'a' is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A person 3300 borrowed at 10% annual simple interest repayable in 2 equal annual installments. What will be the annual installment?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; 10% &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; 3300 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2319; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; 2 &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 1600", "Rs. 1200", "Rs. 1100", "Rs. 1400"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 1600", "&#2352;&#2369;. 1200", "&#2352;&#2369;. 1100", "&#2352;&#2369;. 1400"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Solution:</p><p>S.I = P * R * T/100</p><p>= 3300 * 10 * 2/100</p><p>= Rs. 660</p><p>A = Amount = 3300 + 660 = Rs. 3960</p><p>T = Time</p><p>R = rate</p><p>Installment = (A * 100)/ [T * 100 + (Tn  1 + Tn  2 +  + 1) * R]</p><p>= (3960 * 100)/ [2 * 100 + (1 + 1) * 10]</p><p>= (3960 * 100)/ 220</p><p>= Rs. 1600</p><p>Hence, annual instalment = Rs. 1600</p><p></p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Solution:</p><p>S.I = P * R * T/100</p><p>= 3300 * 10 * 2/100</p><p>= Rs. 660</p><p>A = Amount = 3300 + 660 = Rs. 3960</p><p>T = Time</p><p>R = rate</p><p>Installment = (A * 100)/ [T * 100 + (Tn  1 + Tn  2 +  + 1) * R]</p><p>= (3960 * 100)/ [2 * 100 + (1 + 1) * 10]</p><p>= (3960 * 100)/ 220</p><p>= Rs. 1600</p><p>Hence, annual instalment = Rs. 1600</p><p></p><p></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>What value should come in place of the question mark?</p><p>(3/4 of 400)  -  (5  X  ?) + &#8731;343 = 14</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2330;&#2367;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p><p>(400 &#2325;&#2366; 3/4) - (5 X ?) + &#8731;343 = 14</p>", "options_en": ["50", "55", "65", "60"], "options_hi": ["50", "55", "65", "60"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>(3/4 of 400)  -  (5  X  ?) + &#8731;343 = 14</p><p>=&gt; 300 - (5  X  ?) + 7 = 14</p><p>=&gt; ? = 300/5</p><p>=&gt; ? = 60</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(3/4 of 400)  -  (5  X  ?) + &#8731;343 = 14</p><p>=&gt; 300 - (5  X  ?) + 7 = 14</p><p>=&gt; ? = 300/5</p><p>=&gt; ? = 60</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>If tan&#952; = 7 + 4&radic;3, then find the value of cosec&#952;sec&#952;.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; tan&#952; = 7 + 4&radic;3, &#2340;&#2379; cosec&#952;sec&#952; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["21", "14", "48", "41"], "options_hi": ["21", "14", "48", "41"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>tan&#952; = 7 + 4&radic;3</p><p>cot&#952; = 1/(7 + 4&radic;3)</p><p>cot&#952; = (7 - 4&radic;3)/[7<sup>2</sup>  -  (4&radic;3)<sup>2</sup>] = 7 - 4&radic;3</p><p>Now,</p><p>tan&#952; + cot&#952; = (7 + 4&radic;3) + (7 - 4&radic;3) = 14</p><p>sin&#952;/cos&#952; + cos&#952;/sin&#952; = 14</p><p>1/sin&#952;cos&#952; = 14</p><p>cosec&#952;sec&#952; = 14</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>tan&#952; = 7 + 4&radic;3</p><p>cot&#952; = 1/(7 + 4&radic;3)</p><p>cot&#952; = (7 - 4&radic;3)/[7<sup>2</sup>  -  (4&radic;3)<sup>2</sup>] = 7 - 4&radic;3</p><p>Now,</p><p>tan&#952; + cot&#952; = (7 + 4&radic;3) + (7 - 4&radic;3) = 14</p><p>sin&#952;/cos&#952; + cos&#952;/sin&#952; = 14</p><p>1/sin&#952;cos&#952; = 14</p><p>cosec&#952;sec&#952; = 14</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>During a school excursion each student of junior school was charged &#8377;325 and each student of senior school was charged &#8377;400. If there were 80 students from junior school and the combined average amount charged per student was &#8377;352, then how many students from senior school went for the excursion?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2370;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#8377;325 &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2368;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#8377;400 &#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2332;&#2370;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; 80 &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2341;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2354;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2369;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#8377;352 &#2341;&#2368;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2368;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2349;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2341;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["55", "45", "50", "40"], "options_hi": ["55", "45", "50", "40"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let number of students in senior school = N</p><p>By the rule of alligation:</p><p><img width=120 height=49 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image060.png\"></p><p>(400  -  352): (352  -  325) = 80: N</p><p>48: 27 = 80: N</p><p>16: 9 = 80: N</p><p>N = 45</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let number of students in senior school = N</p><p>By the rule of alligation:</p><p><img width=120 height=49 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image060.png\"></p><p>(400  -  352): (352  -  325) = 80: N</p><p>48: 27 = 80: N</p><p>16: 9 = 80: N</p><p>N = 45</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>A dishonest trader claims to sell his goods at the cost price, but he uses a faulty weighing scale, earning a 30% profit. Instead of using the correct weight for 1 kilogram, he uses a lighter weight. If the profit gained is 30%, what weight is the trader using for 1 kilogram of goods?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2312;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2366;&#2357;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2357;&#2361; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2379;&#2359;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2340;&#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2370; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 30% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351;, &#2357;&#2361; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2311;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2375;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 30% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2311;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2375;&#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["825.6 gm", "772.5 gm", "769.2 gm", "780.4 gm"], "options_hi": ["825.6 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "772.5 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "769.2 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "780.4 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the price of 1 gm of the article be Rs. 1.</p><p>Let suppose he uses the weight of Q gm for 1 kg</p><p>Cost price of Q gm = Q * 1 = Rs. Q</p><p>Selling price of Q gm = 1000 * 1 = Rs. 1000</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(1000  -  Q)/Q * 100 = 30</p><p>3Q = 10000  -  10Q</p><p>13Q = 10000</p><p>Q is approximately equal to 769.2</p><p>For 1 kg, he uses a weight of 769.2 gram.</p><p><b>Express method : </b></p><p>In terms of price the dealer sells at cost price then CP : SP = 1 : 1, at the end gain 30% through faulty weight,</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Customer get</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Customer paid</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">In price</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">In weight</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">x</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Y</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Net profit</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">20</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">26</td></tr></table><p>So, x : y = (26 * 1) : (20 * 1) = 26 : 20</p><p>Now 26 unit = 1000 g</p><p>Then, 20 unit = 1000/26 * 20 = 769.23 gram.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the price of 1 gm of the article be Rs. 1.</p><p>Let suppose he uses the weight of Q gm for 1 kg</p><p>Cost price of Q gm = Q * 1 = Rs. Q</p><p>Selling price of Q gm = 1000 * 1 = Rs. 1000</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(1000  -  Q)/Q * 100 = 30</p><p>3Q = 10000  -  10Q</p><p>13Q = 10000</p><p>Q is approximately equal to 769.2</p><p>For 1 kg, he uses a weight of 769.2 gram.</p><p><b>Express method : </b></p><p>In terms of price the dealer sells at cost price then CP : SP = 1 : 1, at the end gain 30% through faulty weight,</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Customer get</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Customer paid</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">In price</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">In weight</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">x</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Y</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Net profit</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">20</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">26</td></tr></table><p>So, x : y = (26 * 1) : (20 * 1) = 26 : 20</p><p>Now 26 unit = 1000 g</p><p>Then, 20 unit = 1000/26 * 20 = 769.23 gram.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The amount received after 8 years on a certain sum of money invested at the rate of 18% simple interest per annum is &#8377;1,220. What was the initial sum invested?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; 18% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; 8 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2343;&#2344; &#8377;1,220 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2341;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377; 500", "&#8377; 480", "&#8377; 420", "&#8377; 450"], "options_hi": ["&#8377; 500", "&#8377; 480", "&#8377; 420", "&#8377; 450"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Amount received = interest + principal</p><p>1220 = (p X 18 X 8)/100 + p</p><p>122000 = p X 18 X 8 + p X 100</p><p>122000 = 244p</p><p>p = &#8377; 500</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Amount received = interest + principal</p><p>1220 = (p X 18 X 8)/100 + p</p><p>122000 = p X 18 X 8 + p X 100</p><p>122000 = 244p</p><p>p = &#8377; 500</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>In the figure given below, BC || QR, &#8736;A = 56&deg;, &#8736;B = 72&deg; and &#8736;P = 34&deg;, then find the measure of &#8736;R.</p><p><img width=162 height=231 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11888/image021.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, BC || QR, &#8736;A = 56&deg;, &#8736;B = 72&deg; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#8736;P = 34&deg; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;R &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=162 height=231 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p11888/image021.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["92&deg;", "102&deg;", "88&deg;", "94&deg;"], "options_hi": ["92&deg;", "102&deg;", "88&deg;", "94&deg;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>In &#8710;ABC:</p><p>&#8736;A + &#8736;B + &#8736;C = 180&deg;</p><p>56&deg; + 72&deg; + &#8736;C = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;C = 52&deg;</p><p>Since BC || QR which means, &#8736;BCA = &#8736;PQR = 52&deg;</p><p>In &#8710;PQR:</p><p>&#8736;P + &#8736;PQR + &#8736;R = 180&deg;</p><p>34&deg; + 52&deg; + &#8736;R = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;R = 94&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In &#8710;ABC:</p><p>&#8736;A + &#8736;B + &#8736;C = 180&deg;</p><p>56&deg; + 72&deg; + &#8736;C = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;C = 52&deg;</p><p>Since BC || QR which means, &#8736;BCA = &#8736;PQR = 52&deg;</p><p>In &#8710;PQR:</p><p>&#8736;P + &#8736;PQR + &#8736;R = 180&deg;</p><p>34&deg; + 52&deg; + &#8736;R = 180&deg;</p><p>&#8736;R = 94&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>The number that should be subtracted from 675 and 870 to get 39 as the GCD is: </p>", "q_hi": "<p>675 &#2324;&#2352; 870 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 39 &#2325;&#2379; GCD &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319; &#2357;&#2361; &#2361;&#2376;: </p>", "options_en": ["14", "12", "16", "10"], "options_hi": ["14", "12", "16", "10"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>When we divide 675 by 39, the quotient is 17, and the remainder is 12.</p><p>When we divide 870 by 39, the quotient is 22, and the remainder is 12.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>When we divide 675 by 39, the quotient is 17, and the remainder is 12.</p><p>When we divide 870 by 39, the quotient is 22, and the remainder is 12.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>A, B, and C together can do a piece of work in 24 days and B alone can do the same piece of work in 96 days. If the efficiency of C is 80% more than the efficiency of B, then find the time taken by A to do the work.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 24 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; B &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 96 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2340;&#2366;, B &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2340;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; 80% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["72 days", "84 days", "80 days", "60 days"], "options_hi": ["72 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "84 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "80 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;", "60 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Total work = L.C.M of 24 and 96 = 96</p><p>Efficiency = Total Work/ Time Taken</p><p>Efficiency of A, B, and C = 96/24 = 4</p><p>Efficiency of B = 96/96 = 1</p><p>Efficiency of C = Efficiency of B * 180/100 = 1 * 180/100 = 1.8</p><p>Efficiency of A = 4  -  (1 + 1.8) = 1.2</p><p>Hence, the time taken by A to do the work = 96/1.2 = 80 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total work = L.C.M of 24 and 96 = 96</p><p>Efficiency = Total Work/ Time Taken</p><p>Efficiency of A, B, and C = 96/24 = 4</p><p>Efficiency of B = 96/96 = 1</p><p>Efficiency of C = Efficiency of B * 180/100 = 1 * 180/100 = 1.8</p><p>Efficiency of A = 4  -  (1 + 1.8) = 1.2</p><p>Hence, the time taken by A to do the work = 96/1.2 = 80 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of speed of Meena and Teena is 6:5 respectively. If they run a race on a track of 138 m, then what part of the length of the race should Meena give Teena as a head start, so that the race ends in a dead heat?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2335;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 6:5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2375; 138 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2335;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2352;&#2326;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2367; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["28 m", "32 m", "19 m", "23 m"], "options_hi": ["28 &#2350;&#2368;", "32 &#2350;&#2368;", "19 &#2350;&#2368;", "23 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>If time of constant, then</p><p>Ratio of speed = Ratio of distance</p><p>Ratio of speed of Meena and Teena = 6:5</p><p>Ratio of distance = 6:5</p><p>Length of race = 138 m</p><p>Required head start = 138*(6  -  5)/6 = 23 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>If time of constant, then</p><p>Ratio of speed = Ratio of distance</p><p>Ratio of speed of Meena and Teena = 6:5</p><p>Ratio of distance = 6:5</p><p>Length of race = 138 m</p><p>Required head start = 138*(6  -  5)/6 = 23 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>A and B entered into a partnership with investments in the ratio 3 : 5. After a few months, A withdrew and collected back his money. At the end of the year, they received profit in the ratio 2 : 5. After how many months did a withdraw?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2344;&#2375; 3 : 5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; A &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2368;&#2404; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; 2 : 5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310;&#2404; A &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["6", "9", "7", "8"], "options_hi": ["6", "9", "7", "8"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the investments of A and B are Rs.3a and Rs.5a respectively. </p><p>Let A withdrew his money back after m months. </p><p>Partnership period = 1 year = 12 months </p><p>Then, profit ratio = A: B = (3a * m): (5a * 12) = 2: 5</p><p>m = 8</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the investments of A and B are Rs.3a and Rs.5a respectively. </p><p>Let A withdrew his money back after m months. </p><p>Partnership period = 1 year = 12 months </p><p>Then, profit ratio = A: B = (3a * m): (5a * 12) = 2: 5</p><p>m = 8</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify the following expression  - </p><p>{150  -  [90/3 + 6 * 2] + &radic;121} + 70% of 200 </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2352;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; - </p><p>{150 - [90/3 + 6 * 2] + &radic;121} + 200 &#2325;&#2366; 70% </p>", "options_en": ["259", "-259", "382", "-382"], "options_hi": ["259", "-259", "382", "-382"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>{150  -  [90/3 + 6 * 2] + &radic;121} + 70% of 200</p><p>=&gt; {150  -  [30 + 12] + 11} + 140</p><p>=&gt; {150  -  42 + 11} + 140</p><p>=&gt; 119 + 140 </p><p>=&gt; 259</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>{150  -  [90/3 + 6 * 2] + &radic;121} + 70% of 200</p><p>=&gt; {150  -  [30 + 12] + 11} + 140</p><p>=&gt; {150  -  42 + 11} + 140</p><p>=&gt; 119 + 140 </p><p>=&gt; 259</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>What number is subtracted from each of 20, 24, 32 and 40, such that all are in proportion in same order?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>20, 24, 32 &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2320;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2351;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["4", "6", "8", "10"], "options_hi": ["4", "6", "8", "10"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number subtracted = n</p><p>Then, (20  -  n): (24  -  n) :: (32  -  n): (40  -  n)</p><p>(20  -  n)(40  -  n) = (32  -  n)(24  -  n)</p><p>800  -  60n + n<sup>2</sup> = 768  -  56n + n<sup>2</sup></p><p>4n = 32</p><p><b>n = 8</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number subtracted = n</p><p>Then, (20  -  n): (24  -  n) :: (32  -  n): (40  -  n)</p><p>(20  -  n)(40  -  n) = (32  -  n)(24  -  n)</p><p>800  -  60n + n<sup>2</sup> = 768  -  56n + n<sup>2</sup></p><p>4n = 32</p><p><b>n = 8</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>A large cubical room of side 6 m is filled with gas and there are two exhaust fans of different size. One is smaller and can exhaust the gas from the room in 18 hours while the other fan is large and can exhaust the gas from the room in 8 hours. Find that the difference between the exhaust rate of smaller fan to that of larger fan is what per cent of exhaust rate of smaller fan?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>6 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2350;&#2352;&#2366; &#2327;&#2376;&#2360; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2319;&#2327;&#2381;&#2332;&#2377;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2366; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2350;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2327;&#2376;&#2360; &#2325;&#2379; 18 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2366; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2350;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2327;&#2376;&#2360; &#2325;&#2379; 8 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2327;&#2381;&#2332;&#2377;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2342;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2346;&#2306;&#2326;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2327;&#2381;&#2332;&#2377;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2342;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["75", "125", "87.5", "112.5"], "options_hi": ["75", "125", "87.5", "112.5"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of room = 6<sup>3</sup> = 216 m<sup>3</sup></p><p>Exhaust rate of smaller fan = 216/18 = 12 m<sup>3</sup>/h</p><p>Exhaust rate of large fan = 216/8 = 27 m<sup>3</sup>/h</p><p>Required percent = [(27  -  12)/12] * 100 = 125%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of room = 6<sup>3</sup> = 216 m<sup>3</sup></p><p>Exhaust rate of smaller fan = 216/18 = 12 m<sup>3</sup>/h</p><p>Exhaust rate of large fan = 216/8 = 27 m<sup>3</sup>/h</p><p>Required percent = [(27  -  12)/12] * 100 = 125%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If x +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&nbsp;&#2351;&#2342;&#2367;  x +&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["87", "81", "77", "79"], "options_hi": ["87", "81", "77", "79"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>x+(1/9x) = 3</p><p>multiply both sides by 3 we get,</p><p>3x + 1/3x = 9</p><p>Squaring both sides we get,</p><p>9x<sup>2</sup> + 1/9x<sup>2 </sup>+ 2 * 3x * 1/3x = 81</p><p>9x<sup>2</sup> + 1/9x<sup>2</sup> = 79</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x+(1/9x) = 3</p><p>multiply both sides by 3 we get,</p><p>3x + 1/3x = 9</p><p>Squaring both sides we get,</p><p>9x<sup>2</sup> + 1/9x<sup>2 </sup>+ 2 * 3x * 1/3x = 81</p><p>9x<sup>2</sup> + 1/9x<sup>2</sup> = 79</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the four-digit number 535y is divisible by 7, then what is the value of y?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 535y, 7 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; y &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["4", "5", "3", "2"], "options_hi": ["4", "5", "3", "2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>If a number is divisible by 7, then the last digit of the number multiplied by 2 and subtracted from the rest of the number, leaving the last digit, will be 0 or a multiple of 7.</p><p>Now check the options,</p><p>Option a: y = 4, so 535  -  8 = 527 not a multiple of 7.</p><p>Option b: y = 5, so 535  -  10 = 525 a multiple of 7.</p><p>So, y = 5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>If a number is divisible by 7, then the last digit of the number multiplied by 2 and subtracted from the rest of the number, leaving the last digit, will be 0 or a multiple of 7.</p><p>Now check the options,</p><p>Option a: y = 4, so 535  -  8 = 527 not a multiple of 7.</p><p>Option b: y = 5, so 535  -  10 = 525 a multiple of 7.</p><p>So, y = 5</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three pipes, P, Q and R, together take four hours to fill a tank. All the three pipes were opened at the same time. After three hours, P was closed, and Q and R filled the remaining tank in two hours. How many hours will P alone take to fill the tank?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;, P, Q &#2324;&#2352; R, &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319;&#2404; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342;, P &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2324;&#2352; R &#2344;&#2375; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; P &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?", "options_en": ["8", "10", "12", "9"], "options_hi": ["8", "10", "12", "9"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>P+Q+R fill a tank in 4 hours</p><p>They worked for 3 hours , so remaining work= 1-3/4=1/4</p><p>Q + R can do 1/4 work in 2 hours:-</p><p>So Q+R can fill whole tank in 4*2=8 hours</p><p>we have 1/P+1/Q+1/R =1/4----(i)</p><p>and 1/Q + 1/R=1/8----(ii)</p><p>So , putting value of eq (ii) in eq(i) we get:-</p><p>1/P=1/4-1/8=4/32=1/8</p><p>So P can alone complete it in 8 hours.</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>P+Q+R fill a tank in 4 hours</p><p>They worked for 3 hours , so remaining work= 1-3/4=1/4</p><p>Q + R can do 1/4 work in 2 hours:-</p><p>So Q+R can fill whole tank in 4*2=8 hours</p><p>we have 1/P+1/Q+1/R =1/4----(i)</p><p>and 1/Q + 1/R=1/8----(ii)</p><p>So , putting value of eq (ii) in eq(i) we get:-</p><p>1/P=1/4-1/8=4/32=1/8</p><p>So P can alone complete it in 8 hours.</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>KLMN is a parallelogram such that &#8736; MKL = X&deg;, &#8736; KML = Y&deg;, and &#8736; KNM = Z&deg;. Find the value of (X + Y + Z).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>KLMN &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#8736; MKL = X&deg;, &#8736; KML = Y&deg;, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#8736; KNM = Z&deg;. (X + Y + Z) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;.</p>", "options_en": ["360&deg;", "90&deg;", "120&deg;", "180&deg;"], "options_hi": ["360&deg;", "90&deg;", "120&deg;", "180&deg;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=233 height=138 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22067/image004.png\" ></p><p>We know that opposite angles of parallelogram are equal.</p><p>So, &#8736; KNM = &#8736; KLM = Z&deg;</p><p>Sum of all angles in a triangle = 180&deg;</p><p>So,</p><p>&#8736; LKM + &#8736; KLM + &#8736; LMK = 180&deg;</p><p>X + Y + Z = 180&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=233 height=138 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22067/image004.png\" ></p><p>We know that opposite angles of parallelogram are equal.</p><p>So, &#8736; KNM = &#8736; KLM = Z&deg;</p><p>Sum of all angles in a triangle = 180&deg;</p><p>So,</p><p>&#8736; LKM + &#8736; KLM + &#8736; LMK = 180&deg;</p><p>X + Y + Z = 180&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Choose the correct statement from the following.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["HCF is the least common multiple of the given numbers.", "HCF of two or more numbers is the highest number which perfectly divides all the given numbers.", "HCF is also called the least common divisor.", "In prime factorization method of HCF, the multiples of all the given numbers are listed."], "options_hi": ["&#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;", "&#2342;&#2379; &#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2357;&#2361; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2340;: &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;", "HCF &#2325;&#2379; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2349;&#2368; &#2325;&#2361;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;", "&#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2357;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2332; &#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368;&#2348;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>HCF is highest common factor of the given numbers, so it is the highest number which perfectly divides all the given numbers.</p><p>Hence, option (2) is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>HCF is highest common factor of the given numbers, so it is the highest number which perfectly divides all the given numbers.</p><p>Hence, option (2) is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>A rice seller makes a 24% profit without changing the cost or selling price, simply because his faulty weighing machine gives only 850 grams instead of 1 kg. If the cost of 1 kg of rice is &#8377;Y, and he switches to a proper machine that correctly weighs 1000 grams, what should be the new selling price (in &#8377;) to maintain the same 24% profit?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2348;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366; 24% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2311;&#2360;&#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2326;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348; &#2340;&#2380;&#2354; &#2350;&#2358;&#2368;&#2344; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; 850 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#8377;Y &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2361; &#2319;&#2325; &#2313;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2358;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2330; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2338;&#2306;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375; 1000 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2340;&#2380;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 24% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319; &#2352;&#2326;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["1.025Y", "1.054Y", "1.086Y", "1.075Y"], "options_hi": ["1.025Y", "1.054Y", "1.086Y", "1.075Y"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Actual C.P = Y * 850/1000 = 0.85Y</p><p>Profit % = (S.P  -  C.P) * 100/C.P</p><p>24 = (S.P  -  0.85Y) * 100/0.85Y</p><p>26.35Y = 25S.P</p><p>S.P = 1.054Y</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Actual C.P = Y * 850/1000 = 0.85Y</p><p>Profit % = (S.P  -  C.P) * 100/C.P</p><p>24 = (S.P  -  0.85Y) * 100/0.85Y</p><p>26.35Y = 25S.P</p><p>S.P = 1.054Y</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of (cosA + cosB)<sup>2</sup> + (sinA  -  sinB)<sup>2</sup>?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>(cosA + cosB)<sup>2</sup> + (sinA - sinB)<sup>2</sup>? &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; ?</p>", "options_en": ["4cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)", "2cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)/2", "2cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)", "4cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)/2"], "options_hi": ["4cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)", "2cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)/2", "2cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)/2", "4cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)/2"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>= (cosA + cosB)<sup>2</sup> + (sinA  -  sinB)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= (cos<sup>2</sup>A + cos<sup>2</sup>B + 2cosA.cosB) + (sin<sup>2</sup>A + sin<sup>2</sup>B  -  2sinA.sinB)</p><p>= (cos<sup>2</sup>A + sin<sup>2</sup>A) + (cos<sup>2</sup>B + sin<sup>2</sup>B) + 2(cosA.cosB  -  sinA.sinB)</p><p>= 1 + 1 + 2cos(A + B)</p><p>= 2[1 + cos(A + B)]</p><p>= 2[1 + 2cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)/2  -  1]</p><p>= 2 * 2cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)/2</p><p>= 4cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)/2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>= (cosA + cosB)<sup>2</sup> + (sinA  -  sinB)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= (cos<sup>2</sup>A + cos<sup>2</sup>B + 2cosA.cosB) + (sin<sup>2</sup>A + sin<sup>2</sup>B  -  2sinA.sinB)</p><p>= (cos<sup>2</sup>A + sin<sup>2</sup>A) + (cos<sup>2</sup>B + sin<sup>2</sup>B) + 2(cosA.cosB  -  sinA.sinB)</p><p>= 1 + 1 + 2cos(A + B)</p><p>= 2[1 + cos(A + B)]</p><p>= 2[1 + 2cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)/2  -  1]</p><p>= 2 * 2cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)/2</p><p>= 4cos<sup>2</sup>(A + B)/2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}]}